        "student_prefix": [
          {
            "content": "The capacity of Karson's home library is 400 books. If he currently has 120 books, how many more books does he have to buy to make his library 90% full?",
            "role": "user"
          }
        ],
        "student_prefix_sha256": "d29b11ae831dd9ba83a3d9975e39cb6949f35d2db7c3a1c1e18bf77f4d49d949",
        "target": "Given:\n- Total capacity of the library = 400 books\n- Current number of books = 120 books\n- Desired fullness = 90%\n\nFirst, calculate 90% of the library's capacity:\n90% of 400 = 0.90 * 400 = 360 books\n\nNext, find out how many more books are needed to reach 360 books:\nBooks needed = Desired number of books - Current number of books\nBooks needed = 360 - 120 = 240 books\n\nSo, Karson needs to buy 240 more books to make his library 90% full.\n\nFINAL: 240",
        "target_sha256": "2ef93f77164c11a76011fd5cea847999befdb41d9c3917b67148ce3a8970da16"
      },
