        ],
        "student_prefix_sha256": "983b176911035e3b21f26f314b3fe1b9b14aec2a8465c08724b76cbd9301b26d",
        "target": "First, I calculate Robert's commission from his sales. His commission is 10% of $23600, which is \\(0.10 \\times 23600 = 2360\\) dollars.\n\nNext, I add his basic salary to his commission to find his total earnings. His total earnings are \\(1250 + 2360 = 3610\\) dollars.\n\nRobert then allocates 20% of his total earnings to savings. The amount he saves is \\(0.20 \\times 3610 = 722\\) dollars.\n\nTo find his monthly expenses, I subtract his savings from his total earnings. His monthly expenses are \\(3610 - 722 = 2888\\) dollars.\n\nFINAL: 2888",
