        "target": "Given the problem, I identified the following quantities and the unknown:\n- Basic salary: $1250\n- Commission rate: 10%\n- Total sales: $23600\n- Savings rate: 20%\n- Monthly expenses: unknown\n\nTo find the monthly expenses, I first calculated the commission earned from sales. The commission is 10% of $23600, which I computed as:\n\\[ 0.10 \\times 23600 = 2360 \\]\n\nNext, I added the basic salary to the commission to get the total earnings:\n\\[ 1250 + 2360 = 3610 \\]\n\nThen, I calculated the amount allocated to savings, which is 20% of the total earnings:\n\\[ 0.20 \\times 3610 = 722 \\]\n\nTo find the monthly expenses, I subtracted the savings from the total earnings:\n\\[ 3610 - 722 = 2888 \\]\n\nI verified the result by ensuring that the sum of the savings and the expenses equals the total earnings:\n\\[ 722 + 2888 = 3610 \\]\n\nThis check confirms the accuracy of the calculation. The operations used are straightforward arithmetic and percentage calculations, which are reliable and reusable for similar problems.\n\nFINAL: 2888",
